-- Source module: ThreeSumApsp.Filter.ThinAll
/-!
# The pruned thin product on all instances, at the parameters of the filtering reduction

allInstancesF(N, D, w, U, x, y, wi, wj, out, fr) tests whether `D^1249 ≤ N^71`, calls the offline
routine offline32 of the programs with rational parameters at `ratParamsF` (`c = 212733/10000`,
`θ = 111731/10⁶`) if so, and the brute force if not.  The program is `programF`:
`program31P ratParamsF` followed by allInstancesF (number 74) and regimeTestF (number 75).  As
`Pruned/AllInstancesP.lean`, at the new parameters.

* It solves the task `thinTask` on all instances (`allInstancesF_solves`), with a polynomial need
  (`allInstancesNeedF_poly`).
* In the regime its time is `O(w D^{0.4296471} (log D + 1) + N² (log D + 1)²/D^{0.0703531})`
  (`allInstancesTimeF_le`).
* `claim_thinProductF`: the thin product in this time for programs of the light language.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Light.Filter

open ThreeSumApsp ThreeSumApsp.Spec Light.Sec4

